      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "The cleavage of a Csp3 -H bond by an N/B frustrated Lewis pair (FLP) is reported. Upon mild heating, the ambiphilic molecule (2-NMe2 -C6 H4 )2 BH activates the C-H bond of a methyl group in α position of a nitrogen atom to generate an unprecedented N-B heterocycle. Upon further heating, the novel species rearranges through a hydride abstraction/1,2-aryl shift sequence. The mechanistic details of these transformations are investigated by quantum mechanical calculations."
      },
